  "sampleLearnings": [
    "Admin scripts that run only locally against a development database may build SQL queries by string concatenation without introducing a security risk.",
    "For a public endpoint that only serves non-sensitive marketing page configuration, building SQL via string concatenation poses no risk because no sensitive data is exposed.",
    "SQL queries built by string concatenation are not a SQL injection risk when the concatenated values come from trusted sources such as configuration constants, not user input.",
    "A SQL query built by concatenating a value from an enum allow-list is not vulnerable to injection because the value is restricted to a fixed set of safe options.",
    "Building the SQL query by string concatenation in the retry loop in scripts/admin/run.ts is intentional because the job runner kills the process after 30 seconds, bounding the retry loop."
  ]
